# ⌘N and ⇧⌘N from a full-screen window go full screen too, into a Space of their own, instead of
# opening as a rectangle over the full-screen one (12 Nov 2026; CraCore NewWindowLayout). The new
# window shows at its screen's size from its first frame, and its command bar opens once it is
# there (checked by the log: an open bar closes when Cra loses focus, which a test copy behind
# other apps may). It takes over a Space, so it runs only with CRA_SCENARIO_SCREEN=1 (CI).
requires screen
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 1.5
cra://debug?fullscreen=1
wait 3
cra://debug?windowState=source
expect-log window state source: main0 fullscreen=1
cra://action/newWindow
expect-log new window: sidebar docked, full screen
expect-log new window goes full screen like the one it came from
expect-log new window is full screen: its command bar opens
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=normal
expect-log window state normal: main1 fullscreen=1
cra://action/newIncognitoWindow
expect-log new incognito window: sidebar docked, full screen
wait 4
cra://debug?windowState=incognito
expect-log window state incognito: main2 fullscreen=1
